upstream/{shared-detector.ts,positional.ts,fingerprint-core.js,detector-codec.ts}
are byte-for-byte copies of the corresponding shared/ upstream files.
shared_detector.bin is byte-for-byte upstream data/shared_detector.bin.
provenance.json records upstream git blob SHA-1, SHA-256 and byte lengths.

bank.json retains only schema, built_at and the model id, display_name,
family, family_name, response_count fields from data/unified_bank.json.
The unchanged binary contains all numeric ranker/reference arrays used by the
shared scoring algorithm. Dropped bank fields cannot affect shared scoring.

catalog.json contains exact IDs and three exact environment-01 challenge
prompts, expected counts 218, 233, 247, from the first three samples of
reference record 653ba610-1f33-40ab-93bc-d05685e87c70 in upstream
 data/unified_reference.jsonl. Empty system prompt. The three response texts
alone are retained in fixtures/reference_samples.json, not the raw dataset.
Do not infer model aliases from provider-reported metadata.

score.ts is a local stdin/stdout adapter. score.mjs bundles its reachable
upstream scoring code with esbuild 0.25.12 (no minification). The adapter
validates input, removes non-scoring metadata, maps a successful upstream
ranking's absent decision to "ranked", looks up the exact target ID, emits
only the documented compact response fields, and adds an explicit closed-set
warning. It does not alter numerical features, ranking, calibration, sample
acceptance or sequence-shape checks. It does not enable partial scoring.
No provider client, server, original CLI, network code or runtime dependency
is included. Type-only upstream imports are erased by esbuild.

Closed-set probabilities are relative to the reference bank, not evidence
establishing actual model identity. No open-set accuracy guarantee applies.
The parity fixture is drawn from training references; it checks faithful
implementation, not generalization. On Node v24.22.0 the original modules
with the full original bank and the embedded bundle with the slim bank
produced exactly equal scores and probabilities for all 63 models.
fixtures/original_expected.json stores that original-module result.

